`Faker.__init__` treats a default `Faker()` as single-locale by building one entry in `_factory_map` and then one element in `_factories`. Attribute access for `fake.first_name` first goes through `Faker.__getattribute__`, but that method only intercepts `"seed"`; for `"first_name"` normal lookup fails and Python falls through to `Faker.__getattr__`, so `__getattr__` is invoked. Inside `__getattr__`, the single-locale branch `if len(self._factories) == 1` returns `getattr(self._factories[0], attr)` directly, so it does not call `_select_factory`; `_select_factory` is only used in the later branch for multi-locale proxying.

